LMN 1
title: All the Terrible Things (Suzu's Song)
artist: Shiori examples
tempo: 66
time: 4/4
key: D major
mood: the culmination; a hymn made of everyone's worst thoughts that is the most beautiful thing in the town; grief and release

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ALL THE TERRIBLE THINGS (Suzu's Song). The true ending, from the moment
// Suzu lets go through the whole epilogue. About 3:45; it loops back to the
// solo glass harmonica.
//
// SUZU'S FIGURE, COMPLETE. Every other cue hides, mocks, marches or breaks
// the figure and leaves its falling E hanging. Here it is the first line of a
// whole song, and we finally hear what comes after it. The hymn is pure
// D-major pentatonic (D E F# A B, the notes of the beads; no G, no C#), in
// the four-line shoka shape a whole town can hum (ki, sho, ten, ketsu):
//
//   ki     D5q E5q F#5q A5q | B5h. E5q~ | E5w | (rest)        the figure, canonical
//   sho    D5q E5q F#5q A5q | B5q. A5e B5q D6q | A5w~ | A5h   she climbs one step further
//   ten    D6h B5q D6q | E6h. D6q | B5q. A5e F#5q A5q | B5w  the summit: the E she always
//                                                           fell to, now reached from below
//   ketsu  D5q E5q F#5q A5q | B5h. E5q~ | E5w | (rest)      the figure again
//
// THE FALLING E NEVER STEPS TO D until the last chord (bar 58), as
// LEITMOTIFS.md asks. Each time it falls it lands on a different floor:
// Em7 (verse 1, after the bare octaves), Fadd9 (verse 2), C (bVII, climax),
// and at the end it is held for three bars over Fadd9 -> G -> Gm6
// (bIII - IV - iv) before it falls to D. The glass harmonica takes that last step itself, with the cello
// (Hinata) stepping E -> D an octave below: they come home together.
//
// HINATA'S KITCHEN CHORD  Fadd9, voiced F3 A3 C4 G4 on the accordion as in
// morning_bread. It sits under the falling E (E over F = Fmaj9, no clash)
// in verse 2, the climax and the coda. Her tune (C5 F5 A5 G5, the head in
// HINATA.md's slow 4/4 mapping) is the counter-melody over it: the cello
// sings it an octave down under Suzu's held E (so F4 sits a major 7th below
// E5), then the flute sings it at its own pitch in the bar where Suzu rests.
// The Bridge lets her tune bend into Suzu's key (C becomes C#). In the coda
// the horns and cellos play it under the last E, and her line ends on E,
// Suzu's note, before both step down to D. Neither wins.
//
// THE WIND CHIME  After the D chord is released, one glass chime: a
// glockenspiel D6 and a softer C#6 a triplet-eighth later, as if the crooked
// clapper hit a second, flat tube. LMN has no microtones, so "a little flat"
// is a tube that rings a semitone under the home note. It is the last sound;
// the loop's first note (the glass D5) is where it was heading.
//
// FORM  60 bars of 4/4, 66 bpm, broadening to 48 at the end; about 3:43
//   Prelude    1-4   solo glass harmonica (celesta strike, ocarina tone,
//                    halo bloom): the figure, then a silence
//   V1 ki      5-8   the town lines it out: wordless choir in octaves, alone
//   V1 sho     9-12  glass and choir together; the strings enter, pp
//   V1 ten    13-16  piano arpeggios and the cello's counter-line join
//   V1 ketsu  17-20  everyone so far; half cadence on A7
//   Bridge    21-24  Hinata: flute over the accordion's kitchen chord and a
//                    harp picking her guitar shape; her tune bends into D
//   V2 ki     25-28  strings take the hymn; the figure's E falls onto Fadd9;
//                    cello sings her head under it, then the flute
//   V2 sho/ten 29-36 strings, choir, violas an octave below at the summit
//   V2 ketsu  37-40  the glass returns; Fadd9 again; timpani, harp, flute
//   Climax    41-54  tutti with tubular bells and timpani; summit E6 at bar 50
//   Coda      55-60  E held over Fadd9 (Hinata on horns and cellos), G, Gm6;
//                    the glass falls to D; then the wind chime
//
// HARMONY (a slash shows the bass)
//   V1 ki: bare octaves in the choir; A7sus4 A7 in the silence of bar 8
//   sho:   D Bm7 | G Em7 | F#m7 Bm7 | Em7 A7sus4
//   ten:   Gmaj7 | A . . A7sus4 | F#m7 | Bm7 Bm7/A
//   ketsu: Gmaj7 | D/F# | Em7 | A7sus4 A7        (glass_hill's harmony for the figure)
//   Bridge: Fadd9 | Fadd9 | G7 | A7sus4 A7
//   Verse 2: ki  D A/C# Bm D/A | G . . Fadd9 | Fadd9 | Fadd9   (F -> D lift)
//            ketsu Gmaj7 | D/F# . . Fadd9 | Fadd9 | Fadd9
//   Climax ki: D A/C# Bm D/A | G . . C | C | A7sus4 A7
//   Coda:   Fadd9 | G (G7 colour) | Gm6 | D | D | (chime)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

track beads      celesta        vol=64 pan=16  reverb=60
track glass      ocarina        vol=60 pan=8   reverb=65
track halo       halo_pad       vol=34 pan=-4  reverb=75
track choir      choir          vol=58 pan=-4  reverb=60
track strings    strings        vol=70 pan=-12 reverb=50
track cello      cello          vol=64 pan=22  reverb=45
track cbass      contrabass     vol=58 pan=6   reverb=40
track piano      piano          vol=56 pan=-22 reverb=45
track harp       harp           vol=50 pan=-32 reverb=50
track flute      flute          vol=72 pan=-16 reverb=40
track accordion  accordion      vol=40 pan=26  reverb=45
track horns      french_horn    vol=54 pan=30  reverb=50
track bells      tubular_bells  vol=44 pan=-26 reverb=65
track timp       timpani        vol=46 pan=-6  reverb=55
track chime      glockenspiel   vol=50 pan=36  reverb=70

// ---- Prelude: the beads, alone --------------------------------------------
section Prelude bars=4
beads       | !mf D5q E5q F#5q A5q | B5h. E5q~ | E5w | R |
glass       | !mp D5q E5q F#5q A5q | B5h. E5q~ | E5w | R |
halo        | !pp D5q E5q F#5q A5q | B5h. E5q~ | E5w~ | E5h rh |

// ---- Verse 1 ---------------------------------------------------------------
section V1_Ki bars=4
// the town lines it out, in octaves; the first chord comes in the silence
choir.hi    | !mp D5q:ah E5q F#5q A5q | B5h. E5q~ | E5w | R |
choir.mel   | !mp D4q:ah E4q F#4q A4q | B4h. E4q~ | E4w | R |
choir       | R | R | R | !pp [G3 D4 E4]h:ah [G3 C#4 E4]h |
cbass       | R | R | R | !pp A1w |

section V1_Sho bars=4
// glass and town together; strings enter under them
